{
 "description": "Slow speed noise on the overnight fit's answer, with no fitting (description; 200 animals, 99,840,000 + i).\n\nThe overnight fit misses the wild type on the roaming speed's 10-s window 90th percentile (4 of 5\npopulations, z -3.08 to -3.21) and on the small lawn's roaming-bout length. C.2's speed output has\nno state-dependent spread, which is what `encoder_speed_noise: ou` was built for: the speed's\nsampling noise follows a slow Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process, so 10-s window speeds spread more.\n\nHere the probe model gains that option, with the speed noise's timescale appended as the vector's\nlast entry (every earlier index unchanged). On the overnight answer, timescales of 0.25 s\n(correlation 0.018, nearly independent), 3, 10, 30 and 100 s: the D_fit families on the small lawn\nand the uniform well (kinematics and activity derived from the small lawn), and the three mutants.\n",
